{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>As they are removed.</b> From those emurim specified in the ox of the shelamim offering. But what is specified in the shelamim offering that is not specified here? Rather, to draw the analogy to shelamim: just as shelamim require their fats, so too this one requires its fats; and just as shelamim bring peace forever, so too this one brings peace forever. And in the slaughtering of consecrated offerings it requires learning from it that we do not derive a matter learned from a learned matter in consecrated offerings, in the chapter \"These are their places\" (Zevachim 49)." "<b>On the liver, on the kidneys. On its head and on its legs.</b> All are expressions of addition, like מִלְּבַד (\"besides\")."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:55.851211686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}